><source>Dev Biol</source><volume>68</volume><fpage>462</fpage><lpage>471</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">437335</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005506-Martindale1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Martindale</surname><given-names>MQ</given-names></name></person-group><year>1986</year><article-title>The organizing role of the D quadrant in an equal cleaving spiralian, <italic>Lymnaea stagnalis</italic>, as studied by UV laser deletion of macromeres at intervals between third and fourth quartet formation.</article-title><source>Int J Invertebr Reprod Dev</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>229</fpage><lpage>242</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005506-Henry2"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henry</surname><given-names>JQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Perry</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Martindale</surname><given-names>MQ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Cell specification and the role of the polar lobe in the gastropod mollusc <italic>Crepidula fornicata</italic>.</article-title><source>Dev Biol</source><volume>297</volume><fpage>295</fpage><lpage>307</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16919619</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005506-Lambert1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lambert</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Nagy</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>MAPK signaling by the D quadrant embryonic organizer of the mollusc <italic>Ilyanassa obsoleta.</italic></article-title><source>Development</source><volume>128</volume><fpage>45</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11092810</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005506-Gonzales1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gonzales</surname><given-names>EE</given-names></name><name><surname>van der Zee</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Dictus</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>van den Biggelaar</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Brefeldin A or monensin inhibits the 3D organizer in gastropod, polyplacophoran, and scaphopod molluscs.</article-title><source>Dev Genes Evol</source><volume>217</volume><fpage>105</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17120024</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005506-Clement2"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clement</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name></person-group><year>1967</year><article-title>The embryonic value of the micromeres in <italic>Ilyanassa obsoleta</italic> as determined by deletion experiments. I. The first quartet cells.</article-title><source>J Exp Zool</source><volume>166</volume><fpage>77</fpage><lpage>88</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005506-Clement3"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clement</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name></person-group><year>1986a</year><article-title>The embryonic value of the micromeres in <italic>Ilyanassa obsoleta</italic> as determined by deletion experiments. II. The second quartet cells.</article-title><source>Int J Invert Reprod Dev</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>139</fpage><lpage>153</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005506-Clement4"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clement</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name></person-group><year>1986b</year><article-title>The embryonic value of the micromeres in <italic>Ilyanassa obsoleta</italic> as determined by del